Jeremy Matthew Toeman <Shaggy+@CMU.EDU> writes:

>Occasionally I get a message "You feel wise, you must have been
>observant" and my wisdom goes up. Sometimes my dexterity too, and
>occasionally they drop..  Why does this happen, and can I control it so
>I can increase all my stats?

There are ways to stear this process, but there are too many to mention
them all. If you want specific information, get the appropriate spoiler
file from the krl site: ftp.krl.caltech.edu:/pub/nethack/WCST/spoil804.

>Should you donate money to a priest of a different god than yours?

Any priest will do if your goal is to increase your AC. If you want to
higher your standing with your god, you should donate LOTS to one of
your own kind, but donating to a non-co-aligned priest will not harm
you (not sure about Moloch's (high) priest).

>If your god gives you several artifact weapons (at altars), can you sell
>the ones you don't want to use, or will that piss him off?

He doesn't care at all. If you think money will better further his
cause than he'll rely on your good judgement.

>How many levels are there in the Gnomish Mines, and what is the overall
>point to them, aside from just gaining much experience?

The number of levels varies, but the deepest averages to 11. The point
is the luckstone that can be found on the lowest level, and the candle
shop in town, which you need to finish the game (you need at least 7
candles).

>When you kick a box/chest, and something shatters, is that always just a
>gem, or could it be valuable things too??

Potions are fragile as well. Not all gems are fragile. Glass is, as
well as SOME gems.

>I killed a gnome, and ate its corpse immediately afterwards, and it was
>already tainted! How could I have known about this?

The number of turns is random (1-50 I think), and could have been 1.

>Is it really worth it to carry around blank scrolls and magic markers if
>I am a barbarian who rarely makes it to the 11th level (experience, not
>depth)?

If you are a barbarian, you shouldn't have problems carrying lots of
things around. You should have a decent strength. Anyway, the more junk
you carry, the less chance that if you have something stolen, it's
something valuable.

